		(descr "Mantech K3599 1/4in (6.35mm) 3-conductor CLOSED (switched) open-frame phone jack, 6 solder lugs. From the datasheet drawing: body 30mm long x 18.5mm wide, 2 lug rows 12mm apart, lugs 1.5x3.0mm, barrel hole O6.5, bushing M9, BARREL AXIS 12mm off the mounting plane. The barrel/bushing is IN LINE with the legs at the +Y end (faces the back wall). Pads 1/2/3 = Tip/Ring/Sleeve (match the Conn_01x03 symbol); the 3 unnumbered pads are the switch lugs (soldered, no net in v1). BOTTOM-MOUNTED: place on B.Cu so the body hangs below the board. @@ VERIFY: the along-length lug pitch (7mm here is ESTIMATED from the drawing) and the Tip/Ring/Sleeve lug assignment (meter the real part) before fab. @@")
